msgid "freeports\\_dev.ci.config"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.config:1 of
msgid ""
"``ci.yaml``: what a repository demands of a commit, in one file with one "
"name everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.config:3 of
msgid ""
"Every freeports repository -- the engine, a formats repository, an input "
"database -- is gated by a file called ``ci.yaml`` at its root, written in"
" one syntax. That is deliberate and it was a reversal: an earlier round "
"of this design put the settings inside each repository's own manifest, "
"``package.yaml`` here and ``metadata.yaml`` there, and the roles of the "
"branches then read differently in every repository. A manifest says *what"
" the repository is*; this file says *how it is gated*, which is a "
"different question with a different audience, and the engine repository "
"-- which has no manifest at all -- would have needed one invented for the"
" purpose."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.config:23 of
msgid ""
"**Absent, everything falls to the defaults**: class ``dev``, no "
"thresholds, the default key server -- which is to say a repository nobody"
" has configured reports and never refuses. That is the right behaviour "
"for a repository nobody has configured yet, and it is why the file's "
"absence is not an error."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.config:28 of
msgid "Two things in it *are* errors, and loudly:"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.config:30 of
msgid ""
"a branch matching two class lists -- resolving that silently would make "
"the class of a commit depend on the order of a mapping nobody reads;"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.config:32 of
msgid ""
"a threshold naming a metric this repository cannot measure -- a threshold"
" that can never be evaluated is a threshold somebody thinks they have."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.config:35 of
msgid ""
"The three tiers are the engine's own, resolved per setting: **command "
"line, then environment, then this file, then the default**. Thresholds "
"are per metric all the way down, so ``--min`` on one metric does not "
"discard the file's minima for the others."
msgstr ""

